  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A small, aristocratic Jewish party of the Second Temple period, closely tied to the high priesthood and the Jerusalem Temple, which held to the written law of Moses, rejected the Pharisees' oral traditions and denied the resurrection of the dead; in the Gospels they question Jesus about the resurrection, and in Acts they lead opposition to the apostles." .
