  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What does Jeremiah tell the exiles to do in Jeremiah 29:4-7, and why might that have surprised people who expected to go home soon?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Psalm 137 asks how anyone can sing the Lord's song in a foreign land. How do Ezekiel 1:1-3 and Isaiah 40:1-2 answer that question in different ways?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Matthew 1:17 divides Jesus's family tree at the exile. What does that tell you about how the first Christians understood where Jesus fits in Israel's story?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/babylonian-exile> .
