  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "According to Exodus 12:26-27, what are parents to tell their children when they ask about the Passover, and why might Israel have built a question into the ritual?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How does Exodus 20:2 connect the commandments to the rescue from Egypt? What difference does it make that God saves first and then gives the law?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Paul calls Christ \"our Passover\" (1 Corinthians 5:7) and says the wilderness events \"happened to them by way of example\" (1 Corinthians 10:11). Where do you see your own story in Israel's — both the rescue and the grumbling afterwards?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#Event> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Exodus" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Exodus from Egypt" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "the deliverance from Egypt" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "the departure from Egypt" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-story-of-the-bible> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "God's deliverance of the Israelites from slavery in Egypt under Moses — through the plagues, the first Passover and the crossing of the sea — which became Israel's defining story of salvation and which the New Testament uses to explain the death and resurrection of Jesus." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scheme/events-and-timeline> .
