  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/binding-of-isaac> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The account in Genesis 22:1-19 of God testing Abraham by asking him to offer his beloved son Isaac on a mountain in the land of Moriah, of Abraham binding Isaac on the altar, and of the angel who stops him, the ram offered in Isaac's place, and God's renewed oath of blessing; Jews call it the Akedah (\"binding\"), and Christians have long read it as a foreshadowing of Christ." .
