  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/psalm-22> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The psalm of David that begins \"My God, my God, why have you forsaken me?\": a lament that moves from feeling abandoned, mocked and surrounded to a vow of praise in which the nations and generations yet unborn turn to God. Jesus prayed its first words from the cross, and the Gospels tell the crucifixion in its language." .
