<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Read Deuteronomy 6:4-5. What does Israel confess about God, and what does God ask for in return? Why do you think the command to love follows straight after the confession?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "List every place and time of day named in Deuteronomy 6:7-9. Which of them are part of your ordinary week, and how could God's words be \"on your heart\" there?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Deuteronomy 6:20-23 a child asks what the commandments mean. How do the parents answer, and what does that suggest about why Israel obeys?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When the scribe asks Jesus which commandment is first (Mark 12:28-32), how does Jesus answer, and what does the scribe add?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Paul writes of \"one God, the Father\" and \"one Lord, Jesus Christ\" (1 Corinthians 8:6). How does this echo the Shema, and what does it say about who Jesus is?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema/check/6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "James 2:19 says even the demons believe that God is one. What is the difference between agreeing with the Shema and living it?" .
