  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/shema> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Deuteronomy 6:4-9, named for its first Hebrew word (\"Hear\"): Israel's confession that the LORD is our God and the LORD is one, joined to the command to love him with all the heart, soul and strength and to keep his words in the heart, the home and daily life. It became the central confession of Jewish prayer, and Jesus quoted it as the first commandment." .
