<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Compare Matthew 6:9-13 with Luke 11:2-4. Which petitions do both share, and what setting does each Gospel give the prayer (Matthew 6:5-8; Luke 11:1)?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The first petitions are about God's name, kingdom and will; the later ones about our bread, our sins and our testing. What does that order teach about how to pray?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Every pronoun in the prayer is plural (\"our\", \"us\"). How does praying it change if I picture my church, or the believers I find hardest to love, praying it with me?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Matthew 6:14-15 Jesus adds a comment on just one petition. Which one, and why might he single it out?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Jesus prays \"your desire be done\" in Gethsemane (Matthew 26:42). How does that scene deepen what it means to pray \"your will be done\"?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#Passage> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Lord's Prayer" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Luke 11:2-4" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Matthew 6:9-13" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Our Father" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Pater Noster" .
