  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Read Exodus 3:6 and Mark 12:26-27 side by side. Why does God's naming himself \"the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob\" matter for whether the dead will be raised?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Luke adds that \"all are alive to him\" (Luke 20:38). How might that line shape the way a Christian thinks about believers who have died?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sadducees-question-about-the-resurrection/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Does Jesus say that the risen become angels, or that they are like angels? Why does the difference matter?" .
