  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/suffering-and-lament> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "where is God when it hurts" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/suffering-and-lament> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "why do I suffer" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/suffering-and-lament> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/prayer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/suffering-and-lament> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "What Scripture says to Christians who are suffering: the Bible does not explain every sorrow, but it gives God's people words to bring their pain, protest and questions honestly to him in lament, as the psalmists, Job, Lamentations and Jesus on the cross did, and it holds that cry together with trust in God's faithful love and the hope of a world made new." .
