<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Every book of the Hebrew Bible except one is represented among the scrolls. Which book is missing, and why might the absence of a book from a small, damaged collection prove very little?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Compare Deuteronomy 32:8 in two English translations. How do they end the verse, and what does the difference tell you about the manuscripts behind them?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Both the Qumran community and Mark 1:2-3 used Isaiah 40:3 about the wilderness. How did each understand the \"way\" being prepared?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How does it affect your confidence in Scripture to learn that a scroll copied before Jesus's birth reads almost exactly like the Isaiah in your Bible, while also showing small differences?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#Manuscript> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/dead-sea-scrolls> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dead Sea Scrolls" .
