  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/masoretic-text> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The traditional Hebrew text of the Old Testament as fixed by Jewish scholars called Masoretes between about the sixth and tenth centuries AD, who added vowel signs, reading accents and marginal notes to the inherited consonantal text; it is the authoritative Bible of Judaism and the basis of most modern Old Testament translations." .
