  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/acts-of-the-apostles/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/acts-of-the-apostles/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Acts 1:8 names Jerusalem, Judea and Samaria, and \"the uttermost part of the earth.\" Trace where the story is in chapters 2, 8, 10 and 28. How does the book follow that map?" .
