  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/acts-of-the-apostles/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Acts ends with Paul under guard in Rome yet preaching \"with all boldness, none forbidding him\" (28:31). Why might Luke end there rather than with Paul's trial, and what does that say about the ongoing story the church still lives in?" .
