<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Read Luke 1:1-4. What does Luke say about how he gathered his material, and why does he say he is writing to Theophilus?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In the synagogue at Nazareth (Luke 4:16-21) Jesus reads from Isaiah 61. Who is the good news for, and what does he say has happened \"today\"?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Luke 15 opens with a complaint that Jesus \"receiveth sinners, and eateth with them\" (15:2). How do the three stories that follow answer it, and why does the last one end with the elder brother still outside?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Luke 10:29 the lawyer asks \"who is my neighbor?\", but in 10:36 Jesus asks which man \"proved neighbor\". How does that change of question change the way you read the parable?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Luke 24 ends with the risen Jesus opening the Scriptures to his disciples (24:27, 44-45). How might reading the Old Testament \"concerning himself\" shape the way you read it this week?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke> .
