  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-luke> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The third Gospel and the first volume of Luke's two-part work with Acts: an orderly account, written for Theophilus, of Jesus' birth, Spirit-anointed ministry, long journey to Jerusalem, death, resurrection and ascension, presenting him as the Saviour who seeks and saves the lost and brings good news to the poor and to all peoples." .
