<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mark 1:1 calls what follows \"the beginning of the gospel of Jesus Christ\". What does the word \"gospel\" mean, and where in Isaiah 40 and 52 does the idea of a messenger with good news come from?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "According to Luke 1:1-4, what did Luke know about earlier accounts and eyewitnesses, and why did he write his own?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "John 20:30-31 says many signs were left out. What does John say his book is for, and how might that purpose shape the way you read any of the Gospels?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospels> .
