  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Saul of Tarsus, a Pharisee who persecuted the first Christians, met the risen Jesus on the road to Damascus and became the apostle to the Gentiles; he planted churches across the eastern Mediterranean, and the letters bearing his name make up nearly half the books of the New Testament." .
