  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/peter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Simon, a Galilean fisherman whom Jesus renamed Cephas or Peter (\"rock\"); first among the Twelve, the disciple who confessed Jesus as the Christ, denied him three times and was restored by the risen Lord, and who then led the early church in Jerusalem and opened its door to the Gentiles before dying, by early tradition, as a martyr in Rome." .
