<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Jeremiah 1:4-10, what objection does Jeremiah raise to God's call, and what two kinds of work (tearing down and building up) is he given?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "According to Jeremiah 7:1-15, why could the Temple not protect the people of Judah, and what did God want from them instead?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What does Jeremiah 29:4-7 tell the exiles to do in Babylon, and how does verse 11 read differently once you know it was written to people facing seventy years away from home?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Read Jeremiah 31:31-34 alongside Luke 22:20 and Hebrews 8:8-13. What is \"new\" about the new covenant, and how do the New Testament writers see it fulfilled?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Jeremiah 20:7-18 the prophet both praises God and curses the day he was born. What does it mean to you that such honest prayers are part of Scripture?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-jeremiah/check/6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Jeremiah buys a field in a city under siege (Jeremiah 32:6-15). Where might God be asking you or your church to act in hope when circumstances look bleak?" .
