<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Read Genesis 1:26-28 and 1:31. What does God say about human beings, and how does he judge everything he has made?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Genesis 2:4 and 37:2 both begin with \"This is the history of the generations of…\". How does noticing this repeated heading help you see the shape of the whole book?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What three things does God promise Abram in Genesis 12:1-3, and who, finally, is to share in the blessing?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Genesis 50:20 Joseph looks back on his brothers' cruelty. What does he say about their intentions and about God's? Where have you seen God bring good out of something meant for harm?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Paul quotes Genesis 15:6 in Romans 4:3 and Genesis 12:3 in Galatians 3:8. Why do you think the apostle reaches back to Genesis to explain the gospel?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Genesis opens with a world declared \"very good\" and closes with a family in a foreign land waiting for God's promise. What does that tell you about where the story is heading?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis/check/6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/genesis> .
