<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What three things does God promise Abram in Genesis 12:1-3, and who, finally, is to be blessed through him?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Genesis 15:6 says Abram believed and it was credited to him as righteousness. What had God just promised him (15:1-5), and what in his circumstances made it hard to believe?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Compare Genesis 12:10-20 and Genesis 16:1-4 with Genesis 22:1-18. What do the earlier stories show about Abraham's fears and shortcuts, and how has his trust grown by chapter 22?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Genesis 18:22-33 Abraham bargains with God over Sodom. What does he appeal to in verse 25, and what does this teach about bold, honest prayer?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Paul (Romans 4) and James (James 2:21-24) both use Abraham. Which episodes does each one point to, and how can both be true at once?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hebrews 11:8 says Abraham \"went out, not knowing where he went.\" Where is God asking you to take a next step before you can see the whole road?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham/check/6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/abraham> .
