  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "According to Exodus 3:7-12, what has God seen and heard, what will he do, and how does he answer Moses' question \"Who am I\"?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What excuse does Moses give in Exodus 4:10, and how does God respond in verses 11-17?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Exodus 32:11-14 and 32:30-32, what reasons does Moses give God for sparing the people? What does his prayer show about the kind of leader he was?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why was Moses not allowed to lead Israel into the land (Numbers 20:7-12)? What exactly had God told him to do, and what did he do instead?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hebrews 3:5-6 calls Moses a faithful servant in God's house and Christ a faithful Son over it. How does that comparison honour Moses rather than dismiss him?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/moses/check/6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Moses argued with God, failed, interceded and kept going for forty years. Where in your own calling do you most identify with his reluctance — or with his perseverance?" .
