  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-temple> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sanctuary of Israel's God on the Temple Mount in Jerusalem: first built by Solomon and burned by the Babylonians, rebuilt after the exile and lavishly expanded by Herod, then destroyed by Rome in AD 70; in Scripture the place where God set his name among his people, a theme the New Testament carries over to Jesus himself and to the church." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-temple> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scheme/places-and-geography> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-temple> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "The Temple" .
