  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Joshua 1:8 says the book of the law should not depart from Joshua's mouth. What does that suggest about how meditation was practised, and what is it meant to lead to?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What did Mary do with the shepherds' words in Luke 2:19, and how is that like the step of meditatio?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Luke 10:38-42, what is Mary doing, what is Martha doing, and why does Jesus defend Mary?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Which movement (reading, meditation, prayer, contemplation or action) comes hardest for you, and how could a small group help you grow in it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#after> "In the scene, Jesus defends Mary for sitting and listening to him while Martha is pulled apart by her serving; he invites me to put listening to him first and to notice where worry crowds it out, and my serving can grow from that." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#before> "Jesus' words to Martha about the one thing needed jumped out at me, so God is telling me to quit the hospitality team." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#situation> "A member of a small group prays through Luke 10:38-42, the visit of Jesus to Martha and Mary, during a busy season of church volunteering." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#why> "Lectio begins by asking what the text says in itself before asking what it says to me, so a striking phrase is heard within its scene instead of as a free-floating private message." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Choose a short passage of a few verses, such as a Gospel scene or a psalm, settle into quiet, and ask God to speak to you through his word." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Lectio - read the passage slowly several times, aloud if you can, and first ask what the text says in itself and where it sits in its chapter." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Meditatio - stay with a word or phrase that stands out, turn it over, and ask what that meaning says to your life today." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Oratio - answer God in your own words, with thanks, confession, questions or requests drawn from the passage." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Contemplatio - rest quietly before God for a few minutes without trying to produce more thoughts." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Actio - choose one concrete way to live out what you received, and test any strong impression against the wider Bible and with your church or small group." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Lectio Divina" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina/howto/6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#Practice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Lectio Divina" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "divine reading" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "lectio" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "prayerful reading of Scripture" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "reading meditation prayer contemplation" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "sacred reading" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/prayer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An ancient Christian way of reading a short passage of Scripture slowly and prayerfully, moving through reading (lectio), meditation (meditatio), prayer (oratio) and contemplation (contemplatio), and often on to action (actio), so that reading the Bible becomes a conversation with God." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scheme/study-practices> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Lectio Divina" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/biblical-interpretation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/inductive-bible-study> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lectio-divina> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context> .
