<https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "According to Psalm 119:11, where does the psalmist keep God's word, and for what purpose?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Deuteronomy 6:6-9 and 11:18, where are God's words to be kept, and in which everyday settings are they to be talked about?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Matthew 4:1-11, how does Jesus answer each temptation, and what does the devil's own use of Scripture show about the difference between knowing words and understanding them?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What does Colossians 3:16 suggest about memorizing Scripture together as a church rather than only alone?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#StudyQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What passage would you most like to carry with you in a hard season, and how could your small group help you learn it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#after> "I'll learn Colossians 3 a few verses at a time, recite it aloud each day, review what I've learned, and ask what each part means in Paul's letter." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#before> "I'll learn fifty unrelated verses this year and quote whichever one fits my mood that day." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#situation> "A new believer wants to start memorizing Scripture and plans to work through a box of single \"promise\" verses printed on cards." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/ontology#why> "Learning a passage within its setting, with daily review and understanding, guards against treating verses as detached slogans or formulas repeated without being understood." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Choose a passage that is a whole unit, such as a psalm, a parable or a paragraph of a letter, and read it in its chapter first so you know what it means." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Learn a small portion at a time, a verse or a sentence, saying it aloud and repeating it until you can recite it without looking." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Add the next portion only when the earlier ones come easily, then recite the whole section from the beginning each day." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Review what you have already learned on a regular schedule, daily at first and then less often, so that it moves into long-term memory." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Pray the words back to God and ask how they shape what you believe and do, so that memorizing leads to meditation and obedience." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Learn with others, for example by reciting a passage together in a small group or with your family." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Scripture Memorization" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-memorization/howto/4> .
